<title>GERMANY: Mannesmann plans statement on TI.</title>
<headline>Mannesmann plans statement on TI.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Mannesmann AG declined to comment on Thursday on market talk it was selling 42 million shares in British engineering company TI Group Plc, but a company spokesman said it would issue a statement shortly.</p>
<p>Market sources said in London earlier that the shares, equivalent to eight percent of TI's share capital, were being placed by brokers UBS, SBC Warburg and Cazenove at 532 pence.</p>
<p>TI shares last traded at 556 pence, down 8-1/2 pence from their previous close. Mannesmann stock was up 5.2 marks at 588 marks on the Frankfurt stock exchange.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
